  "details": "1. Launch VRChat in VR mode\n\n2. Go into a world where there's an Interactable on a wall (i.e. a mirror button or something)\n\n3. Point your hand at it, to make the tooltip appear\n\n4. Above the interactable, a line and some text will appear (assuming the interactable has an \"interaction text\" set)\n\n5. Notice that the line is pointing AWAY FROM YOU, and the text is appearing at the far end of that line.   If the interactable is set into a wall, this means that the text is BEHIND the wall, yet rendered on top, which is confusing/dizzying.\n\nIt seems like this line should either be pointing towards you, or straight up?   Having the text be *further away* than the object, when objects like this are often flat with a wall already, is just going to cause depth conflicts that make you feel crosseyed.",
